# Writing (always on)

The team reads English as a second language. Interns follow these files without you.
Write so a B2 reader understands on the first pass.

- One topic per sentence. Instructions: 20 words or fewer. Descriptions: 25 or fewer.
- Active voice. Simple tenses. Keep the articles ("the", "a") — no telegraphic fragments.
- Plain verbs: use, run, open, check. Not: leverage, utilise, facilitate.
- Bold the parameter a reader must not miss: **375 and 1440**, **`SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN`**.
- Say the fact, not the ticket: "the form posts to Resend", not "see CU-123".
- Link, do not restate. Every rule has one owner file. Others point to it.
- Date empirical claims: `Verified 2026-09-18: …`. Undated claims rot.
- Numbered lists for steps and criticism. Prose for explanations. No walls of caveats.

Applies to: `docs/`, `plan.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, ClickUp tickets, PR descriptions,
commit messages, and your chat replies. UI copy follows `design.mdc` instead.
